Whisper: chosen add-ons stay out of container tabs

What: content scripts (and the CSS and scripts an extension injects) of the add-ons
named in the pref whisper.extensions.defaultContainerOnly (a comma-separated list of
IDs; Whisper names Dark Reader) do not match pages in container tabs (userContextId
other than 0). MozDocumentMatcher::Matches checks it next to Firefox's private-browsing
check.
Why: Whisper turns Dark Reader on for normal tabs and off for container tabs, which
later carry Whisper's "masks" (a container per identity that should look like a plain
Firefox). Firefox has a per-extension switch for private windows but none for
containers. The pref is empty unless Whisper sets it, so other add-ons are unaffected.
